        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 28 at 2:34PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Daytime high temperatures will reach 70 to 75 degrees throughout\nthis week, and will be hottest on Wednesday and Thursday.\nTemperatures this warm, and for this long, happen about once per\nyear.\n\nThe long duration of warmer days may impact subsistence\nactivities like berry picking, fishing, and hunting. This could\nalso affect people who are extremely sensitive to heat (like\nelders or infants), especially if they are unable to cool down or\nstay hydrated.\n\nActions: Keep homes cool by closing curtai",
